index 4479b53..96b225e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,32 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Browser agent tools
+
+The shared layout exposes client-side [WebMCP tools](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api)
+when the browser provides `document.modelContext` (or the earlier `navigator.modelContext`).
+Browsers without WebMCP retain the regular search and reading-list UI.
+
+- `list_articles`: article metadata and URLs.
+- `search_articles`: case-insensitive title and summary search with a required `query`.
+- `get_current_article`: the open article’s slug, title, summary, body text and URL; returns an error on other pages.
+- `get_reading_list`: saved article metadata for the current session.
+- `update_reading_list`: required `slug` and `action` (`add` or `remove`); repeated actions keep the same state.
+- `open_search` and `open_reading_list`: open the corresponding flyout and wait for its form to appear.
+
+The open flyouts also expose declarative tools: `search_articles_form` (`query`) and
+`update_reading_list_form` (`slug`, `action`). Both use ordinary labeled form controls,
+submit without navigation, and return structured results through the native submit event’s
+`respondWith` method when invoked by an agent. Closing a flyout removes its form tool;
+the imperative utilities remain available throughout Astro client navigation.
+Reading-list changes use the existing session API and notify mounted bookmarks and flyouts.
+
+Run client helper and tool registration checks without a server or browser:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/browser-tools.test.mjs
+pnpm run build
+```
+
+The tests use Node 24’s TypeScript stripping and mock the browser APIs and network requests.
